
  <sn><md>### Changing DNS in Ubuntu

First go to this [website](https://dnsspeedtest.online/) and check your dna speed.Select your convenient dns with low ping value


1. Find your connection name:

```bash
nmcli connection show
```

2. Suppose your connection is `Wired connection 1`:

```bash
sudo nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.dns "1.1.1.1 9.9.9.9"
```

3. Reconnect:

```bash
sudo nmcli connection down "Wired connection 1"
sudo nmcli connection up "Wired connection 1"
```

4. Verify:

```bash
nmcli device show | grep DNS
```

You should see something similar to:

```text
IP4.DNS[1]: 1.1.1.1
IP4.DNS[2]: 9.9.9.9
```</md></sn>
